# Live per-user state never belongs in the shared repo; copy STATE.template.md
# into your projects instead.
STATE.md
# Same reason: the work registry records real working paths, which can be
# home directories or client and project names on someone's machine.
threads/
.DS_Store
*.bak*
__pycache__/
.superpowers/
# Build artifacts from `uv build` or `python3 -m build`. They must never be
# committed and they must never be left lying around either: scripts/
# verify-install.sh walks the tree and fails on any entry the manifest does
# not name, so a forgotten build/ directory makes a clean checkout look
# tampered with. See docs/PACKAGING.md.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
# Generated per-project documentation. Same reason as STATE.md and
# threads/ above: the pages render live store rows, real claimed paths,
# owner names and note authors, which are one machine's working state and
# not shared repository content. Regenerate it with
# `python3 tools/bm_docs.py generate` in any project, including this one.
Documentation/
# V2 (release-closure loop2 refuter fixes): tools/bm_project.py's generated
# views, same reason as STATE.md and Documentation/ above (real project
# rows, not shared repository content). Root-anchored (a leading "/") so
# only THIS repo's own top-level copies are ignored; project-template/'s
# CANVAS.md and DELIVERY-PACKET.md are the shipped template a fresh project
# starts from and stay tracked. The plain and the multi-project
# (CANVAS-<project_id>.md, see C5) filenames are both covered.
/CANVAS.md
/DELIVERY-PACKET.md
/CANVAS-*.md
/DELIVERY-PACKET-*.md
